WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Choose a seated posture that feels stable.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:13.860
If you are very sleepy, unwell, or responsible for driving or another safety-critical task, rest or address that need instead of relying on meditation to create alertness.

3
00:00:21.191 --> 00:00:24.451
Let the spine find a little length without becoming rigid.

4
00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:28.141
Feel both feet or the full base of support.

5
00:00:29.841 --> 00:00:33.501
Stability begins below while attention becomes clearer above.

6
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.740
Open the eyes enough to receive light.

7
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.670
Let the gaze rest forward and slightly down.

8
00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:57.960
Notice color, edges, and depth without staring at one object.

9
00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.454
Feel one ordinary inhale.

10
00:01:16.154 --> 00:01:17.624
Do not make it deeper.

11
00:01:19.324 --> 00:01:25.424
Notice where the body expands or lifts, then let the exhale return without collapsing the posture.

12
00:01:40.697 --> 00:01:42.207
Bring attention to sounds.

13
00:01:43.907 --> 00:01:47.267
Hear the nearest sound, then the farthest one available.

14
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:50.927
Let listening widen the sense of the room.

15
00:02:09.256 --> 00:02:11.366
Notice temperature on the face and hands.

16
00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:18.736
Coolness, warmth, moving air, or no clear difference can all serve as fresh information.

17
00:02:34.009 --> 00:02:39.169
Press the feet lightly into the floor or the body into its support, then release the extra effort.

18
00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:44.839
Feel the brief increase in contact and the return to ordinary pressure.

19
00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:07.037
Roll the shoulders slowly once if movement is comfortable.

20
00:03:08.737 --> 00:03:10.407
Let the head balance over the spine.

21
00:03:12.107 --> 00:03:14.697
Alertness can include movement rather than fighting it.

22
00:03:29.971 --> 00:03:32.761
Choose three breaths to meet at their beginning.

23
00:03:34.461 --> 00:03:39.411
Each time an inhale first becomes noticeable, recognize: a new breath is here.

24
00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:06.839
If thought becomes foggy, sharpen one channel at a time.

25
00:04:08.539 --> 00:04:09.669
See one edge clearly.

26
00:04:11.369 --> 00:04:13.199
Hear one sound clearly.

27
00:04:14.899 --> 00:04:16.899
Feel one point of contact clearly.

28
00:04:38.282 --> 00:04:41.772
Now include all three: seeing, hearing, and touch.

29
00:04:43.472 --> 00:04:47.492
Let the field be bright enough to stay interested and broad enough to remain settled.

30
00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:13.045
Notice whether alertness has become tension in the jaw, brow, or hands.

31
00:05:14.745 --> 00:05:18.045
Soften unnecessary effort while keeping the eyes and posture awake.

32
00:05:36.373 --> 00:05:39.103
Bring to mind the first useful task of the day.

33
00:05:40.803 --> 00:05:43.503
Name it in a few concrete words.

34
00:05:45.203 --> 00:05:48.023
Avoid loading it with the whole day's expectations.

35
00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:06.286
Imagine beginning only the first visible step.

36
00:06:07.986 --> 00:06:11.326
Feel the feet and one breath as you picture that beginning.

37
00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.535
Return to immediate sensation.

38
00:06:33.235 --> 00:06:35.865
Light, sound, contact, breath.

39
00:06:37.565 --> 00:06:41.485
Let these signals organize attention without demanding enthusiasm.

40
00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:09.858
Take one slightly fuller stretch only if it feels natural: lengthen the arms, lift the chest, or move the neck gently.

41
00:07:11.558 --> 00:07:14.018
Then settle into a steady upright shape.

42
00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:31.121
Look around the room deliberately.

43
00:07:32.821 --> 00:07:34.711
Name where you are and what comes next.

44
00:07:36.411 --> 00:07:39.641
Orientation turns wakefulness toward a real situation.

45
00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.310
Move into the next part of the day at a workable pace.

46
00:07:56.010 --> 00:08:00.000
You practiced being awake without becoming hurried and grounded without becoming dull.
